WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.650
Before that, one map of
every non-person identity.

2
00:00:03.650 --> 00:00:08.518
The four AD kinds, service accounts,
M S As, g M S As and d M S As,

3
00:00:08.518 --> 00:00:14.868
live only in Active Directory, and
they're described only by AD attributes;

4
00:00:14.868 --> 00:00:17.725
none of them carries an Azure tag.

5
00:00:17.725 --> 00:00:22.767
Everything else lives in Entra I D:
app registrations, managed identities,

6
00:00:22.767 --> 00:00:28.387
federated credentials and agent identities,
each described by attributes on the

7
00:00:28.387 --> 00:00:33.925
object, such as its owners, the record it
points to, and custom security attributes.

8
00:00:33.925 --> 00:00:36.963
Tags come in only where
there's an Azure resource:

9
00:00:36.963 --> 00:00:41.900
a user-assigned managed identity, or the
Arc machine behind a server's identity.

10
00:00:41.900 --> 00:00:43.212
The difference matters.

11
00:00:43.212 --> 00:00:45.475
Attributes are fields on the object.

12
00:00:45.475 --> 00:00:48.327
Tags are plain-text labels
that Azure tools read,

13
00:00:48.327 --> 00:00:50.537
and they're never a security boundary.

14
00:00:50.537 --> 00:00:53.400
Now, how attributes reach applications.
